Z||000008||b lo 0||08-02-2000||11:57 AM||||Yeah, fixer-uppers are great.  It gives you a sense of it being YOUR car.  My '85 GT I picked up Saturday is a fixer upper.  Needs<BR> sail panels (ordered)<BR>headlights (ordered)<BR>wing (talking to Coop)<BR>repair on fascia<BR>new hinge pins (already done)<BR>work on driver's PDL actuator (in progress)<BR>some vinyl warpage repair (in progress)<BR>right rear NB taillight cover (going to U Pull It saturday)<BR>Seals and Weatherstripping (ordered)<BR>Battery Tray (looking-anyone?)<BR>P-A-I-N-T!!!  (not anytime soon)<P>But, it'll be well worth it when I'm done.<BR><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">    <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
